/**
@page verification_and_ci Verification and CI

@tableofcontents

@section verify_commands Reproducible local checks

Run these from the library root:

| Check | Command | What it proves |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Library build | `make` | Both families archive with no warnings; four archives in total. |
| Empty target set | `make TARGETS=` | The recursive build tolerates no selected family. |
| Device database | `make genlinktests` | The six linker-script cases in `ld/tests/` generate correctly. |
| Public API | `make apitest` | Every public prototype compiles and links with `-Werror`. |
| Style second opinion | `make stylecheck` | checkpatch findings are clean, with formatter-only exceptions documented in the Makefile. |
| Formatting | `clang-format --dry-run -Werror` | The tracked C sources match the repository formatting authority. |
| Documentation | `make html` | Root and both family Doxygen sites generate with empty warning logs. |

@section verify_ci CI matrix

The library CI builds the combinations that would catch family-specific flags
or headers leaking into the shared build:

* 3 toolchains × 2 families;
* both families in a single `make` invocation;
* a freestanding/without-newlib job;
* an examples job that clones `libopenwch-examples` and builds all seven examples
  against the current checkout.

The satellite repositories have their own CI for the application skeleton,
examples, and host-side flasher.

@section verify_hardware Hardware-in-the-loop

There is an explicit gap in the current verification: the code has been built,
linked, and statically checked, but not exercised on real silicon.  A
WCH-LinkE and target boards are required to verify:

* blink and UART echo on CH32V003 and CH582;
* the complete `wchlink` flash sequence on a real CH32V003;
* CH58x flash support, whose ROM-resident routine is not yet implemented.

Until those runs are done, the documentation should not describe hardware
behaviour as verified.

@section verify_generated_files Generated files

The following are generated by `scripts/irq2nvic_h` and must never be edited
by hand:

* `include/libopenwch/<family>/nvic.h`
* `lib/<family>/vector_handlers.c`
* `lib/<family>/vector_names.c`

Run `make irq` to regenerate them.  This target needs no RISC-V toolchain and is
also the first step of `make html`.
*/
